{
  "_comment": "ENGRAM config schema v2. Lives at $ENGRAM_HOME/config.json. Hand-edit fields below to tune; run tools/migrate_config_v2.py to upgrade an older config to this shape. tools/sync-cron.sh renders the user's crontab from cadence below.",

  "schema_version": 2,

  "trust_pool": [
    "reuters.com",
    "apnews.com",
    "bloomberg.com"
  ],
  "yellow_domains": [],
  "confidence_map": {
    "hard_data": 0.95,
    "official_statement": 0.85,
    "attributed_analysis": 0.7,
    "unnamed_source": 0.5,
    "personal_communication": 0.4,
    "editorial": 0.35
  },
  "predictive_confidence_cap": 0.6,
  "chain_decay": 0.95,
  "corroboration_decay": 0.98,
  "resolution_confidence_threshold": 0.7,

  "memory": {
    "decay_base": 1.014,
    "current_turn": 0,
    "tier1_max_nodes": 200,
    "tier2_max_nodes": 1000
  },

  "embedding": {
    "model": "all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
    "enabled": true
  },

  "user": {
    "timezone": "America/New_York"
  },
  "primary_user": "you",

  "_comment_fairy_policy": "Fairy delegation policies — how the agent decides whether to spawn a fairy vs. do the work directly. Both default to 'auto'. Values: 'explicit' (spawn only when user asks), 'auto' (agent judges per-task using the named skill), 'always' (unconditionally delegate). In 'auto' mode the agent loads the skill engram-auto-coder-fairy-judgement or engram-auto-reviewer-fairy-judgement to decide; edit those skill files to tune the heuristic.",
  "coder_fairy_policy": "auto",
  "reviewer_fairy_policy": "auto",

  "cadence": {
    "_comment_cadence": "Cron + drowsiness tunables. heartbeat_minutes is a list of minute-of-hour values to fire heartbeat (e.g., [0, 30] = twice an hour). sleep_hour/minute is when the daily sleep cycle fires in user.timezone. sleep_protected_window_minutes is how wide a window around sleep that heartbeat avoids — render_cron.py computes per-slot skips from this window (no separate skip-list config). drowsiness_caution_pct/urgent_pct trigger context_tracker warnings.",

    "_comment_multi_agent": "Multi-agent stagger: each agent has its own config.json with its own cadence — render_cron.py does NOT auto-stagger. To run two agents on the same host without overlapping schedules, edit heartbeat_minutes and sleep_minute per agent directly. Worked example (Lei's setup): Borges uses sleep_hour=20, sleep_minute=30, heartbeat_minutes=[0, 30]; Mneme uses sleep_hour=20, sleep_minute=15, heartbeat_minutes=[15, 45]. The 15-min offset puts the two sleep cycles sequential (Mneme 20:15 → Borges 20:30) instead of concurrent.",

    "heartbeat_minutes": [0, 30],
    "sleep_hour": 20,
    "sleep_minute": 30,
    "sleep_protected_window_minutes": 60,
    "drowsiness_caution_pct": 80,
    "drowsiness_urgent_pct": 90
  }
}
